   1	# voice_echo
   2	
   3	On-demand raw PCM record-then-playback test application for the contest board.
   4	
   5	```text
   6	nsh> voice_echo
   7	nsh> voice_echo --once
   8	nsh> voice_echo recordmem
   9	```
  10	
  11	The default and `--once` commands immediately record exactly five seconds from
  12	I2S0 RX, play the captured PCM once through I2S1 TX, and return to NSH.
  13	`recordmem` records at most three seconds and enters ASR directly. GPIO14 is not connected
  14	on the current contest board, so this application does not use GPIO14, GPIO0,
  15	or `/dev/buttons`.
  16	
  17	OLED state transitions are best-effort. Playback uses `REC 5 SEC` -> `PLAY` ->
  18	`DONE`; `recordmem` uses `REC 3 SEC` -> `ASR REQ` -> `ASR DONE`.
  19	OLED failures are reported but do not abort audio.
  20	
  21	Audio profile: 16 kHz input, 24 kHz output, mono, 16-bit samples in 16-bit
  22	slots. The rates come from `eda-robot-pro/config.h`; sample width, slot width,
  23	and external module behavior are provisional and not hardware-validated.
  24	The record buffer is derived as `16000 * 5 * sizeof(int16_t)` (160000 bytes).
  25	Playback performs the existing 16 kHz to 24 kHz 3:2 conversion in DMA-sized
  26	chunks, so it does not allocate a second complete playback buffer.
  27	
  28	`recordmem` is the board-side voice-pipeline stage. It records at most three
  29	seconds of the same 16 kHz mono PCM, builds a standard 44-byte WAV header in
  30	RAM, and immediately submits the PCM buffer to the registered ASR backend. No
  31	path argument, filesystem, `fopen`, or `fwrite` is used. The WAV header is kept
  32	as an in-memory view for the next audio stage; the ASR interface receives the
  33	PCM portion because its contract is 16-bit LE, 16 kHz, mono PCM.
  34	
  35	When `CONFIG_EXAMPLES_AI_AGENT_VELA` is enabled, `recordmem` initializes the
  36	voice channel on demand and performs one synchronous ASR request. The
  37	recognized text is printed, then the command returns to NSH. If ai_agent is
  38	disabled, the command reports `ASR unavailable` after recording.

