# Machine-dog voice tools

`mimo_robot_voice_once.py` is the one-shot host tool for the contest robot:

```text
input WAV -> MiMo ASR -> concise machine-dog LLM reply -> MiMo TTS WAV
```

It reuses the request format and bounded response parsing from
`mimo_voice_api_probe.py`. The command performs one transaction and exits; it
does not run a daemon, start board services, or store the API key.

This is the PC/API stage: `--play` uses a player on the host machine. It does
not claim to capture from INMP441 or drive MAX98357; those board-side steps
remain a separate firmware integration and hardware-validation stage.

## Run once

From the workspace root, with the already validated token in the environment:

```sh
export MIMO_API_KEY='...'
python3 contest2026_295_suanliheidong/tools/mimo_robot_voice_once.py \
  --wav contest2026_295_suanliheidong/test.wav \
  --output /tmp/robot_reply.wav
```

The default input is `contest2026_295_suanliheidong/test.wav` and the default
output is `./robot_reply.wav`. Output includes recognized/reply character
counts and the generated WAV path; it does not print the text contents. Add
`--play` only when the host
has `aplay`, `ffplay`, or `paplay` available.

The input is mono PCM16 WAV. 16 kHz is sent unchanged; the board's 24 kHz
speaker-rate WAV (including the checked-in `test.wav`) is normalized to 16 kHz
for ASR. Other sample rates are rejected. TTS audio is validated as a WAV
before it is written. A failure prints only a stage and sanitized error code;
the token, request body, and response body are never printed.

