contest2026_295_suanliheidong/logs/foamzzz/2026-08-10/codex__019fe9f4-0cc1-7022-ac65-6d3a95946af1.jsonl:1:{"schema_version":"1.0","session_id":"019fe9f4-0cc1-7022-ac65-6d3a95946af1","team_id":"contest2026_295_suanliheidong","github_login":"foamzzz","tool":"codex","seq":1,"ts":"2026-08-10T04:36:51.018Z","role":"user","text":"请先阅读：\n\ncontest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/checkpoints/\nminimal_n16r8_nsh_boot/CODEX_HANDOFF.md\n\n以及：\n\ncontest2026_295_suanliheidong/docs/hardware_work.md\n\n把 CODEX_HANDOFF.md 视为已经验证过的项目背景，不要重新回溯旧问题。\n\n读取完成后检查当前 git status/branch，然后从 Minimal NSH known-good baseline 继续 Stage 2 Peripheral Bring-up。\n\n除非 handoff 与当前仓库实际状态冲突，否则不要重新调查 HAL、esptool、Simple Boot 和 Minimal NSH 启动历史。\n我们已经冻结并备份了一个已验证成功的基线：\n\nESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 Minimal NSH Boot\n\n当前基线已经确认：\n- N16R8 PASS\n- Flash 16MB PASS\n- PSRAM 8MB Octal configured\n- UART0 TX43 / RX44 PASS\n- NSH PASS\n- -j8 build PASS\n- nuttx.bin PASS\n- hardware boot -> nsh> PASS\n\n现在进入下一阶段：\n\nStage 2: Peripheral Bring-up\n\n注意：\n本阶段不是实现产品功能。\n本阶段目标仅仅是把 hardware_work.md 中已经确定的硬件外设正确适配到 NuttX b…2183 tokens truncated…oard_pwm.c\nboard_i2s.c\n\n但不要为了文件数量拆分而拆分。\n\n优先复制 NuttX board architecture，\n不是复制具体参考板功能。\n\n每个功能必须：\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_xxx\n\n保护。\n\n功能未启用时仍必须保持 Minimal NSH 可构建。\n\n==================================================\n6. Kconfig / defconfig\n==================================================\n\n更新 contest_board 自己的：\n\nKconfig\ndefconfig\nMake.defs\nboard header\n\n仅启用本阶段真正需要的底层 driver。\n\n不要启用：\n\nWi-Fi\nBluetooth\nLCD\nCamera\nLVGL\ngraphics\naudio application\nnetwork\ncodec\nrecord/play apps\n\n注意：\n\n“I2S driver enabled”\n\n不等于：\n\n“audio feature enabled”。\n\n本阶段可以启用底层 I2S，\n但不要引入整个 multimedia stack。\n\n目标仍然是最小 Peripheral Bring-up firmware。\n\n==================================================\n7. 每个阶段都必须保持可启动\n==================================================\n\n不要一次写完所有外设再 build。\n\n内部执行顺序：\n\nbaseline\n→ GPIO\n→ build\n→ I2C\n→ build\n→ PWM\n→ build\n→ I2S RX\n→ build\n→ I2S TX\n→ final build\n\n但是：\n\n不要每次 build 都向我输出长报告。\n\n自己完成迭代。\n\n如果某一步导致编译失败：\n只修当前 board configuration/board code。\n\n禁止用修改 nuttx/arch/HAL 来快速绕过。\n\n==================================================\n8. 构建方式\n==================================================\n\n必须：\n\ncd ~/vela/openvela\nsource myenv/bin/activate\n\n使用：\n\ncontest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/scripts/build_with_hal_backport.sh -j8\n\n不要直接使用普通 build.sh 代替最终验收。\n\n确保仍然：\n\n- HAL base =\n  9fc713a95b1ff150dd0b0647e465d3c624056bb1\n\n- temporary upstream backport =\n  454d82c70ed\n\n- build 后 HAL 自动 REVERTED\n\n- HAL tracked diff clean\n\n- 不重新加入 --use_segments\n\n==================================================\n9. final image 验证\n==================================================\n\n完成 Stage 2 后：\n\nsource myenv/bin/activate\n\npython -m esptool \\\n  --chip esp32s3 \\\n  image-info \\\n  nuttx/nuttx.bin\n\n必须继续满足：\n\nESP32-S3\n16MB\nDIO\n40m\nchecksum valid\n\nROM RAM segments 必须继续是正常：\n\n0x3fc...\n0x403...\n\n绝不能重新出现：\n\n0x00000020\n0x00010000\n0x00020000\n\n作为 ROM load segment。\n\n==================================================\n10. 不进行硬件功能测试\n==================================================\n\n本轮到“编译 + board adaptation + device registration”结束。\n\n不要：\n\n- 转动舵机\n- 播放声音\n- 录音\n- 点 OLED\n- 实现触摸录音业务\n- Wi-Fi\n- Bluetooth\n- 修改应用层\n\n最多给出以后可以在 NSH 中用于验证 device registration 的命令。\n\n真正硬件功能测试等下一阶段。\n\n==================================================\n11. README\n==================================================\n\n更新：\n\ncontest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/README.md\n\n增加：\n\nPeripheral Bring-up\n\n记录：\n\nGPIO4        LED\nGPIO14       Touch Button\nGPIO0        Boot Button\n\nGPIO12       I2C0 SDA\nGPIO13       I2C0 SCL\nI2C freq     400kHz\n\nGPIO9        Servo PWM\nGPIO10       Servo PWM\nGPIO21       Servo PWM\nGPIO47       Servo PWM\nGPIO48       Servo PWM\nPWM freq     50Hz\n\nGPIO16       MIC BCLK\nGPIO17       MIC WS\nGPIO18       MIC DIN\n\nGPIO38       SPK WS\nGPIO39       SPK BCLK\nGPIO40       SPK DOUT\n\n以及：\n\n实际 I2S0/I2S1 分配。\n\n同时明确：\n\nNOT IMPLEMENTED YET:\n- OLED controller\n- microphone functional capture\n- speaker functional playback\n- servo motion\n- application behavior\n- Wi-Fi\n- Bluetooth\n\n==================================================\n12.…66823 tokens truncated…al_lock_backport.sh`\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/build_with_hal_backport.sh`\\n+\\n+Flow: verify base → temporary apply → build → automatic revert → HAL clean.\\n+\\n+Do not upgrade the whole HAL: newer HAL directory layouts do not match the\\n+current NuttX `hal.mk`. Do not directly modify or commit HAL tracked source.\\n+\\n+DO NOT REMOVE THIS BACKPORT WITHOUT A VALID UPSTREAM-COMPATIBLE SOLUTION.\\n+\\n+# Critical esptool Fix\\n+\\n+The old custom wrapper injected `--use_segments` / `--use-segments` into\\n+`elf2image`. That made ELF Program Header PhysAddr values `0x20`, `0x10000`,\\n+and `0x20000` become ROM load addresses, causing `StoreProhibited` at\\n+`EXCVADDR=0x00000020`.\\n+\\n+Current `scripts/esptool.py` does not inject either flag. It executes\\n+`sys.executable -m esptool` from the active virtualenv and preserves the NuttX\\n+`--ram-only-header` image mode. NEVER REINTRODUCE `--use_segments` FOR THIS\\n+IMAGE FLOW.\\n+\\n+# Boot Image Model\\n+\\n+This is NuttX Simple Boot with one image: `nuttx.bin`.\\n+\\n+- Flash offset: `0x000000`\\n+- Flash size: 16MB\\n+- Flash mode: DIO\\n+- Flash frequency: 40m\\n+- Do not add ESP-IDF `bootloader.bin`, partition table, or OTA data.\\n+\\n+# Image Validation\\n+\\n+After building, before flashing:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+cd ~/vela/openvela\\n+source myenv/bin/activate\\n+python -m esptool --chip esp32s3 image-info nuttx/nuttx.bin\\n+```\\n+\\n+Validated image facts:\\n+\\n+- Entry point: `0x40374f2c`\\n+- DRAM segment: `0x3fc8b840`\\n+- IRAM segment: `0x40374000`\\n+- Flash size: 16MB\\n+- Mode: DIO\\n+- Frequency: 40m\\n+- Checksum: valid\\n+\\n+ROM RAM segments must be in valid `0x3fc...` / `0x403...` ranges. Never accept\\n+`0x00000020` as a ROM load segment.\\n+\\n+# Flash Procedure\\n+\\n+Only after image-info passes:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+cd ~/vela/openvela\\n+source myenv/bin/activate\\n+python -m esptool \\\\\\n+  --chip esp32s3 --port /dev/ttyUSB0 --baud 460800 \\\\\\n+  write-flash --flash-size 16MB --flash-mode dio --flash-freq 40m \\\\\\n+  0x000000 nuttx/nuttx.bin\\n+```\\n+\\n+# UART Wiring\\n+\\n+- USB-TTL RXD → GPIO43\\n+- USB-TTL TXD → GPIO44\\n+- USB-TTL GND → board GND\\n+- Do not connect USB-TTL 3V3/5V to power the board.\\n+- Power the board from an independent stable 5V supply.\\n+\\n+USB-TTL board power previously caused `BROWNOUT_RST`; do not restore it.\\n+\\n+# Known Non-blocking Boot Message\\n+\\n+Simple Boot may print:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+SHA-256 comparison failed\\n+Attempting to boot anyway...\\n+```\\n+\\n+Hardware verification showed that boot continued to `*** Booting NuttX ***`\\n+and `nsh>`. Treat this as non-blocking for this baseline; do not introduce an\\n+ESP-IDF bootloader to suppress it.\\n+\\n+# Modification Boundaries\\n+\\n+Long-term board maintenance is limited to:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+contest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/**\\n+```\\n+\\n+Do not directly maintain tracked changes in `nuttx/**`, `vendor/**`,\\n+`packages/**`, or HAL. Read them for reference only; do not patch arch/HAL to\\n+work around a board feature.\\n+\\n+# Important Board-specific Change\\n+\\n+`src/board_bringup.c` returns `0` on the successful path. Do not change it to\\n+`return OK;` unless a verified header supplies `OK` and the change is needed.\\n+\\n+# Minimal Baseline Files\\n+\\n+- `board/contest_board/README.md` — human build and validation guide\\n+- `board/contest_board/configs/nsh/defconfig` — minimal board configuration\\n+- `board/contest_board/src/board_boot.c` — empty early/late board hooks\\n+- `board/contest_board/src/board_bringup.c` — successful no-op bring-up\\n+- `board/contest_board/src/board_appinit.c` — optional boardctl hook\\n+- `board/contest_board/src/contest_board.h` — board bring-up prototype\\n+- `board/contest_board/patches/0001-esp-hal-nuttx-lock-initializer.patch` — HAL backport\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/esp_hal_lock_backport.sh` — apply/revert guard\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/build_with_hal_backport.sh` — official build entry\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/esptool.py` — active-venv esptool launcher\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/Make.defs` — board linker/toolchain settings\\n+- `board/contest_board/include/board.h` — board include surface\\n+\\n+# Next Stage\\n+\\n+Next stage: **Stage 2 - Peripheral Bring-up**.\\n+\\n+Use `contest2026_295_suanliheidong/docs/hardware_work.md` as the hardware map.\\n+Resources to investigate, without implementing them in this checkpoint:\\n+\\n+- GPIO4 LED\\n+- GPIO14 touch/button input\\n+- GPIO0 boot button input\\n+- I2C0: SDA GPIO12, SCL GPIO13, 400kHz\\n+- Servo PWM/LEDC: GPIO9, GPIO10, GPIO21, GPIO47, GPIO48 at 50Hz\\n+- MIC I2S: BCLK GPIO16, WS GPIO17, DIN GPIO18\\n+- Speaker I2S: WS GPIO38, BCLK GPIO39, DOUT GPIO40\\n+\\n+Prioritize driver/resource/register adaptation. Do not immediately implement\\n+OLED graphics, servo motion, recording, playback, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, or product\\n+application logic.\\n+\\n+Reference board families:\\n+\\n+- `nuttx/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/esp32s3-devkit`\\n+- `nuttx/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/esp32s3-box`\\n+- `nuttx/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/esp32s3-eye`\\n+- `nuttx/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/esp32s3-korvo-2`\\n+\\n+# Unknown Hardware Details\\n+\\n+`hardware_work.md` does not establish the OLED controller/address, exact\\n+microphone chip, or speaker amplifier/codec. Do not guess SSD1306, SH1106,\\n+INMP441, MAX98357, ES8311, or another part number. Start only with verified\\n+GPIO, I2C, PWM, or I2S resources when Stage 2 begins.\\n+\\n+# New Session Rules\\n+\\n+1. Read this file first.\\n+2. Read `docs/hardware_work.md` next.\\n+3. Check contest branch and Git status.\\n+4. Treat Minimal NSH as a known-good baseline; do not re-investigate HAL,\\n+   esptool, boot, or NSH history unless live facts disagree.\\n+5. Create a new peripheral branch before Stage 2 work; do not develop directly\\n+   on `checkpoint/minimal-n16r8-nsh`.\\n+6. Do not add features to this checkpoint.\\n+\\n+# Git / Checkpoint\\n+\\n+- Checkpoint path: `board/checkpoints/minimal_n16r8_nsh_boot`\\n+- Checkpoint branch: `checkpoint/minimal-n16r8-nsh`\\n+- Contest HEAD: `d31d5e6c9897b639d8b78d271149a7b6bec41f34`\\n+- NuttX HEAD: `76354c637858ecb0aa4601629327acb6f44a26bb`\\n+- HAL HEAD: `9fc713a95b1ff150dd0b0647e465d3c624056bb1`\\n+- Recommended future branch: `feature/peripheral-bringup`\\n+\\n+Do not create that future branch as part of this handoff.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","output":null,"is_error":false}
